without my pills,

57
00:04:30,166 --> 00:04:32,752
I'm just keeping my eyes closed.

58
00:04:33,961 --> 00:04:36,589
I'm blocking out visual stimuli

59
00:04:36,672 --> 00:04:39,425
to trick my brain
into thinking I'm sleeping.

60
00:04:39,509 --> 00:04:41,344
You might actually sleep
if you don't talk.

61
00:04:43,846 --> 00:04:47,058
Geez, you're being quite harsh
to someone with insomnia.

62
00:04:47,141 --> 00:04:47,975
You heard that?

63
00:04:57,110 --> 00:04:59,445
How long have you been
taking sleeping pills for?

64
00:04:59,529 --> 00:05:01,364
It seems like it's been a long time.

65
00:05:03,699 --> 00:05:05,451
How would you know that?

66
00:05:20,258 --> 00:05:22,051
How did you know

67
00:05:22,135 --> 00:05:24,303
that I've been taking them
for a long time?

68
00:05:25,096 --> 00:05:27,849
I majored in chemistry.

69
00:05:28,474 --> 00:05:30,143
No wonder why.

70
00:05:30,226 --> 00:05:33,146
I knew you weren't the humanities type.

71
00:05:33,229 --> 00:05:34,522
Then, what's the STEM type like?

72
00:05:35,773 --> 00:05:37,316
The type who points out every detail.

73
00:05:38,526 --> 00:05:40,111
I can hardly say anything around you.

74
00:05:40,194 --> 00:05:42,697
Those pills suppress
the central nervous system,

75
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,740
so you need to be careful
with long-term use.

76
00:05:45,741 --> 00:05:48,619
Are you showing off your expertise?

77
00:05:48,703 --> 00:05:52,456
Ms. Dam, the side effects
aren't something to take lightly either.

78
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,917
Hallucinations, sleepwalking, and--

79
00:05:56,752 --> 00:06:00,631
