Just kidding.

85
00:06:20,026 --> 00:06:21,027
We're here.

86
00:06:24,572 --> 00:06:25,573
Ms. Dam.

87
00:06:30,161 --> 00:06:31,454
Ms. Dam--

88
00:06:32,288 --> 00:06:33,497
What?

89
00:06:33,581 --> 00:06:34,540
We're here.

90
00:06:37,126 --> 00:06:38,419
I wasn't asleep.

91
00:06:39,003 --> 00:06:40,463
-Yes, you were.
-No, I wasn't.

92
00:06:41,088 --> 00:06:42,965
-I said you were.
-I said I wasn't asleep.

93
00:06:44,342 --> 00:06:46,594
You called my name like…

94
00:06:46,677 --> 00:06:49,263
-four times.
-It was three times. Get out.

95
00:06:54,227 --> 00:06:56,145
Oh, right. We…

96
00:06:57,772 --> 00:06:59,440
We should exchange numbers

97
00:06:59,523 --> 00:07:01,651
if we're going to meet
every day until the show.

98
00:07:06,405 --> 00:07:10,368
There's no need for that.
Let's pick a set time and place instead.

99
00:07:11,369 --> 00:07:12,286
AUGUST

100
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:15,122
As you can see, I have no idea
where I'll be at any time.

101
00:07:22,129 --> 00:07:25,508
I won't contact you for any other reasons,
so just give me your number.

102
00:07:25,591 --> 00:07:26,634
Okay?

103
00:07:31,764 --> 00:07:34,559
Goodness, thank you so much.

104
00:07:44,318 --> 00:07:45,570
Could you open the door?

105
00:07:45,653 --> 00:07:47,738
-It's open.
-It is?

106
00:07:47,822 --> 00:07:49,240
You're right.

107
00:07:49,323 --> 00:07:50,491
But why isn't it working?

108
00:07:50,575 --> 00:07:52,243
It's not opening.

109
00:07:52,326 --> 00:07:54,328
Why are you so impatient?

110
00:07:55,371 --> 00:07:56,914
It opens if you push slowly.

111
00:08:08,426 --> 00:08:10,344
Get home safe then.

112
00:08:17,518 --> 00:08:20,563
Gosh, he startled me.

113
00:08:23,316 --> 00:08:25,526
MATTHEW

114
00:08:30,239 --> 00:08:33,534
MR. MECHOORI

115
00:08:38,789 --> 00:08:40,499
MR. MECHOORI

116
00:08:40,583 --> 00:08:41,751
BORN AND RAISED IN DEOKPUNG

117
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:45,588
GOOD MORNING
HAVE A GREAT DAY

118
