165
00:13:29,622 --> 00:13:30,623
You…

166
00:13:30,706 --> 00:13:31,915
Hey.

167
00:13:34,585 --> 00:13:36,670
Do you still have dreams
about the military?

168
00:13:37,296 --> 00:13:38,380
Was it a full night's rest?

169
00:13:38,464 --> 00:13:39,673
You're still not awake.

170
00:13:39,757 --> 00:13:42,009
Company, attention!

171
00:13:51,602 --> 00:13:52,853
I'm heading out.

172
00:13:52,936 --> 00:13:54,480
Hey, stay a bit longer.

173
00:13:54,563 --> 00:13:57,566
Let me feed you something.
How about a fancy restaurant?

174
00:13:58,233 --> 00:13:59,068
Hold on…

175
00:14:06,533 --> 00:14:08,077
Renewal?

176
00:14:09,745 --> 00:14:11,080
L'ÉTOILE
ERIC SEO

177
00:14:11,163 --> 00:14:12,956
You're renewing the contract?

178
00:14:23,717 --> 00:14:25,135
-Are you up now?
-Yeah.

179
00:14:25,219 --> 00:14:26,929
-Let me use some of your lotion.
-Sure.

180
00:14:38,273 --> 00:14:39,525
-Sung-mi.
-Yeah?

181
00:14:39,608 --> 00:14:41,485
How was I during the night?

182
00:14:42,277 --> 00:14:43,195
What do you mean?

183
00:14:43,278 --> 00:14:45,155
Well, I mean…

184
00:14:45,239 --> 00:14:46,532
Did I…

185
00:14:47,324 --> 00:14:48,409
toss and turn

186
00:14:49,034 --> 00:14:51,620
or talk in my sleep?

187
00:14:52,663 --> 00:14:55,165
Or did I walk around or anything?

188
00:14:55,874 --> 00:14:57,084
You slept like a log.

189
00:14:58,669 --> 00:15:00,004
Right?

190
00:15:00,963 --> 00:15:02,798
I knew it.

191
00:15:09,722 --> 00:15:11,140
I told you I'm heading to the farm.

192
00:15:11,223 --> 00:15:13,851
Just have one bite. Just one.

193
00:15:17,187 --> 00:15:18,147
Thank you for the food.

194
00:15:23,610 --> 00:15:24,820
I guess you like it.

195
00:15:25,529 --> 00:15:27,823
Have those rocks in your heart
dislodged now?

196
00:15:27,906 --> 00:15:29,992
You said I couldn't stop it
from happening anyway.

197
00:15:31,076 --> 00:15:32,411
Are you giving her the mushrooms?

198
00:15:35,914 --> 00:15:37,249
I think Ms. Dam

199
00:15:37,791 --> 00:15:38,792
is someone I can trust.

200
00:15:38,876 --> 00:15:39,877
Right.

201
00:15:43,005 --> 00:15:45,507
Were you with sweetie last night?

202
00:15:47,301 --> 00:15:48,635
What?

203
00:15:48,719 --> 00:15:51,388
I didn't see your car around this morning.

204
00:15:51,472 --> 00:15:53,640
I slept at the office.

205
00:15:53,724 --> 00:15:56,810
And stop trying to put
Ms. Dam and I together.

206
00:15:57,352 --> 00:15:59,396
I've treated you to a meal,

207
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:02,274
so you'd better give me
a wedding invitation soon.

208
00:16:05,569 --> 00:16:06,737
Ma'am!

209
00:16:08,280 --> 00:16:09,281
Here, drink some water.

210
00:16:19,792 --> 00:16:21,710
FINALLY IN KOREA

211
00:16:22,294 --> 00:16:24,505
IN 9 DAYS

212
00:16:30,594 --> 00:16:33,013
A SINGLE MIRACULOUS DROP,
AMAZING SKIN TRANSFORMATION

213
00:16:38,310 --> 00:16:40,687
DAM YE-JIN'S ONLY1
L'ÉTOILE LA FIN ESSENCE

214
00:16:48,695 --> 00:16:52,116
Everything's great about this essence,

215
00:16:52,199 --> 00:16:53,534
except for this.

216
00:16:53,617 --> 00:16:55,285
There are some complaints about the pump.

217
00:16:55,369 --> 00:16:56,578
It leaks often,

218
00:16:56,662 --> 00:16:58,539
and many reviews say the suction is weak,

219
00:16:58,622 --> 00:17:00,707
so it won't work at all
once it's about half used.

220
00:17:01,291 --> 00:17:02,376
To be honest,

221
00:17:02,459 --> 00:17:05,170
I also switched it with a different pump
that fits the bottle.

222
00:17:07,631 --> 00:17:10,092
I think this is a pretty important issue.

223
00:17:10,175 --> 00:17:11,760
What do you think?

224
00:17:11,844 --> 00:17:13,846
You're not asking us
to switch the pumps, are you?

225
00:17:13,929 --> 00:17:15,514
Will it be possible?

226
00:17:16,140 --> 00:17:18,767
The pumps were made using a custom mold

227
00:17:18,851 --> 00:17:20,727
that reflects L'Étoile's identity.

228
00:17:20,811 --> 00:17:25,274
Does L'Étoile prioritize its identity
over customer convenience?

229
00:17:28,193 --> 00:17:29,736
Hang on.

230
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:30,654
What?

231
00:17:32,447 --> 00:17:33,907
This isn't a one-time thing.

232
00:17:33,991 --> 00:17:35,826
So it's all okay
just because it's L'Étoile?

233
00:17:35,909 --> 00:17:37,286
Just hang on.

234
00:17:37,369 --> 00:17:39,788
So, Mr. Seo…

235
00:17:40,706 --> 00:17:44,501
Did you see the ads they put up
in the building on the way here?

236
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:46,211
Yes.

237
00:17:46,295 --> 00:17:49,506
Then, you must have seen
my name in large font on them too.

238
00:17:49,590 --> 00:17:50,549
I did.

239
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:52,676
Now that I have my name on it,

240
00:17:52,759 --> 00:17:55,304
disappointing customers
with L'Étoile products

241
00:17:55,387 --> 00:17:57,764
will be a blow to my pride.

242
00:17:59,975 --> 00:18:03,187
If you just switch the pumps,

243
00:18:04,104 --> 00:18:07,065
I really think I can introduce this
to everyone with confidence.

244
00:18:11,069 --> 00:18:12,696
We'll switch them.

245
00:18:12,779 --> 00:18:15,574
So please introduce it
as the perfect essence.

246
00:18:18,076 --> 00:18:19,912
Thank you so much, Mr. Seo.

247
00:18:26,919 --> 00:18:29,546
Where did you go
in such a hurry last night?

248
00:18:31,048 --> 00:18:32,174
I had something to do.

249
00:18:32,257 --> 00:18:33,217
At that late hour?

250
00:18:35,886 --> 00:18:37,012
By any chance,

251
00:18:37,763 --> 00:18:39,890
did you get any calls
from an unknown number?

252
00:18:39,973 --> 00:18:42,184
I always get calls from unknown numbers.

253
00:18:43,101 --> 00:18:46,813
From Jamie in the US,
from Mr. Kim guaranteeing high returns…

254
00:18:46,897 --> 00:18:48,398
Don't even get me started.

255
00:18:50,359 --> 00:18:53,695
Ms. Dam will contact you as well.

256
00:18:53,779 --> 00:18:55,072
I left her your number.

257
00:18:55,864 --> 00:18:57,366
Why?

258
00:18:57,449 --> 00:19:00,494
Did Ms. Dam ask for my number?

259
00:19:00,577 --> 00:19:01,453
Did her network say

260
00:19:01,536 --> 00:19:03,038
-they needed my help?
-No.

261
00:19:03,622 --> 00:19:06,625
Something came up,
so we have to communicate through you

262
00:19:06,708 --> 00:19:08,919
for about ten days
until the broadcast ends.

263
00:19:09,002 --> 00:19:10,921
Please tell me when she contacts you.

264
00:19:11,672 --> 00:19:12,673
Fine.

265
00:19:12,756 --> 00:19:14,925
Sorry for not telling you in advance.

266
00:19:15,008 --> 00:19:16,510
I'd appreciate the help.

267
00:19:18,053 --> 00:19:22,057
Well, you never tell me anything
in advance or apologize anyway…

268
00:19:22,975 --> 00:19:25,018
Mr. Park, aren't you going to work?

269
00:19:25,936 --> 00:19:27,604
There's only one shovel.

270
00:19:28,230 --> 00:19:29,815
We can't offer a discount,

271
00:19:29,898 --> 00:19:32,276
so we'll have to focus
on brand power this time.

272
00:19:32,359 --> 00:19:35,529
We can still emphasize that it's 15%
cheaper than ordering from overseas.

273
00:19:35,612 --> 00:19:37,739
-That's important.
-It is.

274
00:19:39,491 --> 00:19:42,202
Where did we put our list
of key selling points?

275
00:19:42,286 --> 00:19:43,662
My coffee tastes like essence.

276
00:19:43,745 --> 00:19:46,999
Let's have some snacks first
before continuing.

277
00:19:48,458 --> 00:19:51,253
As I said before,
we're going to have to communicate

278
00:19:51,336 --> 00:19:54,381
and follow up with the PR team
to promote the broadcast.

279
00:19:54,464 --> 00:19:56,800
WELCOME TO HIT HOMESHOPPING, L'ÉTOILE

280
00:19:56,883 --> 00:19:58,510
Do we have anything left on our agenda?

281
00:19:58,593 --> 00:20:00,220
Having delicious desserts?

282
00:20:09,146 --> 00:20:12,149
I'm sure you didn't return
just to give us desserts.

283
00:20:13,317 --> 00:20:15,110
What brings you here?

284
00:20:15,193 --> 00:20:16,111
I came to see you.

285
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:21,700
I can't even joke around.

286
00:20:21,783 --> 00:20:22,951
I brought some news.

287
00:20:23,827 --> 00:20:26,246
I just met with our packaging supplier.

288
00:20:26,330 --> 00:20:29,458
We decided to start off
with 10,000 bottles for the launch at HIT.

289
00:20:30,167 --> 00:20:31,543
That's actually great news.

290
00:20:31,626 --> 00:20:35,464
Then, I'll be selling L'Étoile's
first-ever limited-edition essence.

291
00:20:35,547 --> 00:20:38,467
Would you ever consider
working for L'Étoile?

292
00:20:39,551 --> 00:20:40,552
You'd better get in line.

293
00:20:43,764 --> 00:20:45,849
Take it. I still have
some work left to do.

294
00:20:52,647 --> 00:20:53,523
Michelle?

295
00:20:53,607 --> 00:20:57,235
My gosh. You really have no shame, do you?

296
00:20:57,319 --> 00:21:00,989
I send you a gift,
and you don't even give me a single call?

297
00:21:01,073 --> 00:21:03,492
If you knew what I gave up
to answer your call,

298
00:21:03,575 --> 00:21:05,660
you wouldn't be able to say that.

299
00:21:05,744 --> 00:21:08,288
Is the Korean launch coming along well?

300
00:21:08,372 --> 00:21:09,247
<i>Yes.</i>

301
00:21:10,374 --> 00:21:11,666
Don't worry.

302
00:21:19,174 --> 00:21:20,342
Yes?

303
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:30,310
Can we talk for a moment?

304
00:21:48,370 --> 00:21:51,540
Are you really going
to launch L'Étoile's essence?

305
00:21:54,709 --> 00:21:55,919
You really are doing it.

306
00:21:56,002 --> 00:21:59,005
By the way you're reacting,
I guess I'm pretty good at what I do.

307
00:21:59,089 --> 00:22:00,257
Quit this right now.

308
00:22:03,093 --> 00:22:04,761
Why should I listen to you?

309
00:22:09,224 --> 00:22:13,103
Ruining my life was enough,
don't you think?

310
00:22:15,564 --> 00:22:17,315
Just because I returned to HIT

311
00:22:17,399 --> 00:22:20,402
doesn't mean that what happened
five years ago is all in the past.

312
00:22:21,611 --> 00:22:23,238
Do you really not know

313
00:22:24,364 --> 00:22:26,074
why I wanted

314
00:22:26,741 --> 00:22:27,826
to do that broadcast?

315
00:22:27,909 --> 00:22:30,579
How can you be so shameless?

316
00:22:30,662 --> 00:22:33,165
You were desperate to debut.
Who are you trying to blame?

317
00:22:35,041 --> 00:22:36,793
Everyone is saying

318
00:22:36,877 --> 00:22:39,379
that you're not
the same Dam Ye-jin as before.

319
00:22:39,462 --> 00:22:40,755
But what are we going to do?

320
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:43,675
You're still the same in my eyes.

321
00:22:48,263 --> 00:22:50,515
Thanks for the advice.

322
00:22:51,308 --> 00:22:52,434
You just made me

323
00:22:54,269 --> 00:22:56,188
really eager to do well this time.

324
00:23:34,142 --> 00:23:38,647
<i>Ms. Dam wants to meet you</i>
<i>at Seoul Municipal Library at 9:00 p.m.</i>

325
00:24:31,741 --> 00:24:33,285
SHE PAINTS HER PICTURE WITHIN MINE

326
00:25:00,562 --> 00:25:02,230
COSMETIC MICROBIOLOGY

327
00:25:47,859 --> 00:25:50,195
Did you block my number, by any chance?

328
00:25:50,987 --> 00:25:52,072
What?

329
00:25:56,910 --> 00:25:58,203
MR. MECHOORI, 2 OUTGOING CALLS

330
00:25:58,286 --> 00:26:00,163
Why weren't you picking up?

331
00:26:04,250 --> 00:26:05,752
I didn't know you called.

332
00:26:15,095 --> 00:26:16,471
Thank you.

333
00:26:17,722 --> 00:26:18,973
I'll see you tomorrow.

334
00:26:35,740 --> 00:26:36,908
Come on…

335
00:26:59,139 --> 00:27:01,182
COSMETIC MICROBIOLOGY

336
00:27:02,934 --> 00:27:05,603
You didn't have to help me this much.

337
00:27:06,521 --> 00:27:07,522
But are you sure

338
00:27:07,605 --> 00:27:09,858
you can read all this
before the broadcast?

339
00:27:10,358 --> 00:27:12,152
You'll barely have time
to learn your script.

340
00:27:13,236 --> 00:27:14,112
My script?

341
00:27:15,071 --> 00:27:17,365
Have you ever seen a Taekwondo athlete

342
00:27:17,449 --> 00:27:20,034
fight during a competition
by doing all the forms in order?

343
00:27:20,118 --> 00:27:22,078
Every second is a battle.
There's no script.

344
00:27:24,956 --> 00:27:26,875
What's wrong? Are you hurt?

345
00:27:28,626 --> 00:27:30,170
I forgot to have dinner.

346
00:27:30,253 --> 00:27:32,130
This is an emergency.

347
00:27:48,438 --> 00:27:49,856
Are you on the run from someone?

348
00:27:49,939 --> 00:27:51,232
Slow down.

349
00:27:52,942 --> 00:27:54,486
It's a habit.

350
00:27:54,569 --> 00:27:56,446
I have about ten meetings a day,

351
00:27:56,529 --> 00:27:58,907
so I just eat food
as if I'm putting in fuel.

352
00:27:58,990 --> 00:28:00,867
No one spends
more than ten minutes filling up.

353
00:28:14,172 --> 00:28:15,381
You're done already?

354
00:28:15,465 --> 00:28:16,382
Yes.

355
00:28:19,385 --> 00:28:20,428
What's that look?

356
00:28:20,512 --> 00:28:23,431
I'm just feeling glad I added
that special clause in the contract.

357
00:28:25,183 --> 00:28:26,935
What do you mean by that?

358
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:31,481
"Seeing her act, I knew Dam Ye-jin
was full of risks." Is that it?

359
00:28:31,564 --> 00:28:34,150
I didn't know you didn't use scripts.

360
00:28:34,234 --> 00:28:36,861
I thought you were just reciting
what your clients gave you.

361
00:28:39,072 --> 00:28:43,117
I only meant that I'm relieved
I got to learn more about you.

362
00:28:47,163 --> 00:28:49,123
What did you think home shopping hosts do?

363
00:28:49,207 --> 00:28:51,251
It's hard to do
an hour-long show without a script.

364
00:28:51,334 --> 00:28:53,211
I'm sure everyone else will be amazed too.

365
00:28:54,170 --> 00:28:55,797
Then,

366
00:28:55,880 --> 00:28:57,715
should I tell you what my secret is?

367
00:29:02,971 --> 00:29:04,639
You just have to love the products.

368
00:29:05,849 --> 00:29:08,601
If you love them, you just want
to keep talking about them.

369
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:13,106
What? Do I seem cool?

370
00:29:15,233 --> 00:29:16,317
Just finish your food.

371
00:29:16,985 --> 00:29:19,153
Do you know how hard farmers had to work

372
00:29:19,237 --> 00:29:22,115
to produce the lettuce and tomatoes
in that sandwich?

373
00:29:22,657 --> 00:29:23,658
Fine.

374
00:29:29,831 --> 00:29:31,708
I feel much better now.

375
00:29:58,026 --> 00:29:59,485
<i>You just have to love the products.</i>

376
00:29:59,569 --> 00:30:02,864
<i>If you love them, you just want</i>
<i>to keep talking about them.</i>

377
00:30:03,615 --> 00:30:04,449
<i>Guys.</i>

378
00:30:05,950 --> 00:30:08,870
I got a 97.6%
on the skin barrier improvement test.

379
00:30:10,079 --> 00:30:11,122
I must be a genius.

380
00:30:11,205 --> 00:30:14,208
You can't achieve that
just by using expensive ingredients.

381
00:30:14,292 --> 00:30:15,501
You know that, right?

382
00:30:15,585 --> 00:30:18,087
Come on, it's 97.6%!

383
00:30:31,809 --> 00:30:32,644
Mr. Lee.

384
00:30:36,272 --> 00:30:38,024
This is our storyboard for the shoot.

385
00:30:38,107 --> 00:30:40,568
I thought it'd be nice
if you took a look before the shoot.

386
00:30:42,612 --> 00:30:44,155
I notified you before,

387
00:30:44,238 --> 00:30:46,240
but please be careful when moving around,

388
00:30:46,324 --> 00:30:47,909
especially with your equipment.

389
00:30:47,992 --> 00:30:49,077
Of course.

390
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:51,579
Don't touch any of the mushrooms directly.

391
00:30:51,663 --> 00:30:54,624
And access to the area
with the original specimen is limited.

392
00:30:55,375 --> 00:30:58,628
Please make sure not to harm
any mushrooms while filming.

393
00:30:58,711 --> 00:30:59,796
Of course, sir.

394
00:30:59,879 --> 00:31:02,340
I'll make sure
to instruct our crew clearly.

395
00:31:03,007 --> 00:31:05,510
Thank you so much
for agreeing to the shoot.

396
00:31:23,111 --> 00:31:24,362
-Ms. Dam.
-Yes?

397
00:31:24,445 --> 00:31:25,947
Here's the final outline.

398
00:31:26,823 --> 00:31:27,657
Sure.

399
00:31:30,660 --> 00:31:33,746
-We marked the revised parts.
-Sorry. Hang on.

400
00:31:34,831 --> 00:31:35,957
Did you forget something?

401
00:31:38,167 --> 00:31:40,003
-I'll hold that.
-Thanks.

402
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:45,967
I think these will feel
and suit the vibe better today.

403
00:31:46,050 --> 00:31:49,053
They seem to suit our concept better too.

404
00:31:56,227 --> 00:31:57,145
Ms. Dam.

405
00:31:57,228 --> 00:31:58,312
Mr. Seo.

406
00:31:58,396 --> 00:31:59,605
Did you get some sleep?

407
00:31:59,689 --> 00:32:01,190
I couldn't sleep a wink.

408
00:32:01,274 --> 00:32:04,110
Were you nervous?
I told you it's nothing special.

409
00:32:04,193 --> 00:32:05,653
The PR team made a request,

410
00:32:05,737 --> 00:32:07,613
-so let me take your photos.
-Sure.

411
00:32:07,697 --> 00:32:11,868
They say it's for a promotional article
to celebrate the launch in Korea.

412
00:32:11,951 --> 00:32:13,411
Good. Smile.

413
00:32:13,494 --> 00:32:14,662
Stand a little closer.

414
00:32:14,746 --> 00:32:17,248
Good! Amazing! Good!

415
00:32:24,213 --> 00:32:25,381
Awesome.

416
00:32:25,465 --> 00:32:26,299
Très bien!

417
00:32:26,382 --> 00:32:27,967
"Très bien"?

418
00:32:29,510 --> 00:32:32,555
Good, good! Excellent!

419
00:32:32,638 --> 00:32:34,932
Is there anything bothering you?

420
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:37,852
-Mr. Lee?
-Yes?

421
00:32:40,730 --> 00:32:41,689
No.

422
00:32:44,817 --> 00:32:45,985
It seems like there is.

423
00:32:47,862 --> 00:32:48,696
How are they?

424
00:32:48,780 --> 00:32:51,574
These don't belong
in the business section.

425
00:32:51,657 --> 00:32:54,160
They should be
in the entertainment section!

426
00:32:55,870 --> 00:32:56,788
They look great.

427
00:32:58,039 --> 00:32:58,873
I'm sorry.

428
00:33:00,249 --> 00:33:01,667
Did you have breakfast?

429
00:33:01,751 --> 00:33:02,668
Yes. What about you?

430
00:33:02,752 --> 00:33:04,337
I did too.

431
00:33:04,420 --> 00:33:06,339
You weren't too nervous to eat, were you?

432
00:33:06,422 --> 00:33:07,715
A little bit…

433
00:33:10,468 --> 00:33:11,469
Nice to see you again.

434
00:33:14,388 --> 00:33:15,598
Right.

435
00:33:16,390 --> 00:33:18,768
We meet again.

436
00:33:29,112 --> 00:33:34,325
Just think of this as giving Ms. Dam
a tour of this raw material farm.

437
00:33:34,408 --> 00:33:36,285
No need to be nervous. Just act natural.

438
00:33:36,369 --> 00:33:38,913
Keep introducing the farm
as you slowly walk on.

439
00:33:38,996 --> 00:33:40,164
Good luck!

440
00:33:40,248 --> 00:33:41,165
Let's go, Mr. Seo.

441
00:33:41,249 --> 00:33:44,210
Okay, ready! Action.

442
00:33:45,211 --> 00:33:46,671
-This way, please.
-All right.

443
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:55,721
Hey, Mechoori.

444
00:33:55,805 --> 00:33:57,390
Don't be nervous.

445
00:33:57,473 --> 00:34:00,893
The camera's faced that way.

446
00:34:00,977 --> 00:34:01,811
The camera angle.

447
00:34:01,894 --> 00:34:04,230
It's not like that.

448
00:34:04,313 --> 00:34:06,440
Don't be silly.
I can tell you're totally scared.

449
00:34:07,191 --> 00:34:09,068
Be careful.
They can still pick up your voice.

450
00:34:09,152 --> 00:34:10,153
Geez.

451
00:34:12,530 --> 00:34:14,532
Okay, your voices
won't be recorded this time.

452
00:34:14,615 --> 00:34:17,326
So just follow the directions I give you.

453
00:34:17,410 --> 00:34:20,538
To the workers in the back,
you can just keep working as normal.

454
00:34:20,621 --> 00:34:24,041
Don't look at the camera
until I say "cut." Keep that in mind.

455
00:34:24,125 --> 00:34:26,252
You two do a handshake first.

456
00:34:28,588 --> 00:34:31,424
No, let's try that again.
You suddenly look so distant.

457
00:34:31,507 --> 00:34:33,551
Give each other a friendly gaze.

458
00:34:33,634 --> 00:34:35,344
Then, shake hands.

459
00:34:35,428 --> 00:34:37,263
How about a bright smile?

460
00:34:37,346 --> 00:34:38,681
Brighter.

461
00:34:39,432 --> 00:34:40,600
Mr. Seo.

462
00:34:41,267 --> 00:34:43,102
Hold on. What's that?

463
00:34:44,061 --> 00:34:45,396
Cut!

464
00:34:45,479 --> 00:34:46,564
Mr. Lee!

465
00:34:47,481 --> 00:34:48,316
Mr. Lee?

466
00:34:48,816 --> 00:34:49,650
Yes?

467
00:34:49,734 --> 00:34:51,569
Don't look at the camera.

468
00:34:51,652 --> 00:34:54,363
You were staring.
Just keep working, Mr. Lee.

469
00:34:55,031 --> 00:34:57,366
What was that? Let's go again.

470
00:34:57,450 --> 00:34:58,701
Mechoori.

471
00:34:58,784 --> 00:35:01,662
The camera's faced this way.

472
00:35:04,123 --> 00:35:07,335
You shouldn't hide though.
Be in the background of the picture.

473
00:35:07,418 --> 00:35:10,171
And by "picture,"
I don't mean like a painting.

474
00:35:11,005 --> 00:35:12,340
All right, I get it.

475
00:35:13,090 --> 00:35:16,302
Okay, Mr. Lee. You just have to harvest
the mushrooms like you always do.

476
00:35:16,385 --> 00:35:18,554
I'll give you some directions as we go.

477
00:35:18,638 --> 00:35:20,223
-Okay.
-Okay?

478
00:35:20,306 --> 00:35:21,474
Let's go.

479
00:35:21,557 --> 00:35:22,475
Ready!

480
00:35:23,351 --> 00:35:24,602
Action.

481
00:35:27,563 --> 00:35:29,023
That was neat. He's good.

482
00:35:29,106 --> 00:35:30,858
Good. Mr. Lee,

483
00:35:30,942 --> 00:35:34,779
how about brushing it off a bit?

484
00:35:34,862 --> 00:35:35,738
All right.

485
00:35:36,530 --> 00:35:39,492
Gosh, we can see the craftsmanship
in those brush strokes.

486
00:35:39,575 --> 00:35:41,244
-There you go.
-That's great, Mr. Lee.

487
00:35:41,327 --> 00:35:44,372
How about harvesting a mushroom up top?

488
00:35:49,460 --> 00:35:51,295
Ms. Dam, what are you doing after this?

489
00:35:52,546 --> 00:35:53,923
This evening?

490
00:35:55,049 --> 00:35:58,177
I have to wrap up and…

491
00:36:00,054 --> 00:36:01,889
Is he crazy?
Those are expensive mushrooms.

492
00:36:10,898 --> 00:36:12,316
What was that?

493
00:36:12,400 --> 00:36:13,567
Did I tell him to crush it?

494
00:36:13,651 --> 00:36:15,194
-No, you didn't.
-I said to harvest it.

495
00:36:15,278 --> 00:36:16,612
No, I just…

496
00:36:16,696 --> 00:36:18,114
Mechoori.

497
00:36:18,614 --> 00:36:20,574
Your face is too frozen.

498
00:36:21,367 --> 00:36:23,077
The camera's just going to
film your hand--

499
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:26,580
It's not because of the camera!
How many times do I have to tell you?

500
00:36:26,664 --> 00:36:28,791
It's not because of the camera! It's not!

501
00:36:29,375 --> 00:36:31,252
I told you I didn't want to do this.

502
00:36:31,877 --> 00:36:33,170
Just because you do NeoTube…

503
00:36:33,254 --> 00:36:34,588
I know what camera angles are.

504
00:36:34,672 --> 00:36:36,674
I know! I know, okay?

505
00:36:36,757 --> 00:36:39,343
Cut! Why don't we take a short break?

506
00:36:39,427 --> 00:36:42,054
-Hey, go settle things down.
-Yes, let's take a short break.

507
00:36:42,138 --> 00:36:43,222
Just for a moment.

508
00:36:43,306 --> 00:36:44,598
Have some drinks, everyone.

509
00:36:44,682 --> 00:36:46,350
-I brought these sweets.
-There's coffee.

510
00:36:46,434 --> 00:36:47,852
It's coffee. This is amazing.

511
00:36:48,894 --> 00:36:51,272
-Thank you, Mr. Seo.
-You're the best, Mr. Seo.

512
00:36:51,355 --> 00:36:52,732
Thank you for the coffee.

513
00:36:52,815 --> 00:36:55,443
-This is expensive stuff.
-Gosh, this is the good kind.

514
00:36:56,277 --> 00:36:57,278
Thank you, sir.

515
00:37:07,913 --> 00:37:10,291
Gojeuneok Bio is buying!

516
00:37:11,125 --> 00:37:12,376
What's that?

517
00:37:16,047 --> 00:37:17,673
Gosh, the chocolate one looks good.

518
00:37:17,757 --> 00:37:19,550
DRINKS ARE ON GOJEUNEOK BIO!

519
00:37:21,677 --> 00:37:22,511
Sir?

520
00:37:22,595 --> 00:37:23,429
But…

521
00:37:24,680 --> 00:37:27,141
Here's your Mechoori iced tea.

522
00:37:27,224 --> 00:37:29,560
-Thank you.
-Enjoy.

523
00:37:29,643 --> 00:37:31,562
-What did you order?
-Unnie's Power.

524
00:37:31,645 --> 00:37:33,898
In that case,
I'd like a Real Jolly Pongpong.

525
00:37:33,981 --> 00:37:35,941
-Those two.
-Thank you.

526
00:37:36,025 --> 00:37:37,568
-Enjoy.
-Thank you.

527
